# Default artifact and image version definitions for the test harness. This file corresponds to
# stage 6 of the configuration loader, so every earlier stage takes precedence over it, and a
# version matrix run supplies one override file per version set.
#
# By default, these definitions track the latest patch releases: the newest Hadoop 3.4 release and
# the newest HBase release on the minor line of the default profile. Tracking patch releases
# captures upstream bug fixes that an older pin would miss; for example, an earlier harness lost
# time to an HBase 2.6.4 defect that was resolved in HBase 2.6.7. The "Re-pinning" section of
# README.md explains how an operator can re-pin a release or profile for a single host without
# modifying this file.
#
# Every line in this file must be a KEY=VALUE assignment, a comment, or blank. The configuration
# loader parses the file as plain text and never sources it as shell code, so all values are
# treated as literals and no expansion is performed.
#
# Four design rules govern the entries in this file:
#   1. Phoenix itself is never downloaded from a remote repository. The container image packages
#      only the artifacts produced by the local Maven build, which scripts/stage-artifacts.sh
#      reads directly from the build output of this source tree, so no entry here defines a
#      Phoenix download.
#   2. This file defines only the default values for version selection rather than the active
#      selections themselves. When no higher-precedence stage defines them, the loader derives
#      PX_PHOENIX_HBASE_PROFILE, PX_DIST_HBASE_VERSION, PX_DIST_HADOOP_VERSION, PX_IMAGE_TAG, and
#      PX_PHERF_IMAGE_TAG from these defaults. Consequently, versions.local.env (stage 7),
#      env/local.env, a --config file, or the process environment can each re-pin any selection.
#   3. Phoenix compiles against the HBase and Hadoop versions declared by the active profile in
#      the root pom.xml, whereas the cluster runs the runtime releases selected here. The chosen
#      HBase release must fall within the version range supported by the compatibility module of
#      the profile, as defined by PX_HBASE_PROFILES in lib/common.sh; both the staging step and
#      the preflight check reject any release outside that range. Because the HBase daemons use
#      the ZooKeeper and Hadoop client JARs shipped inside lib/ of the HBase distribution archive,
#      and the staging step extracts them directly from that archive, no entry here names them.
#   4. Every downloaded artifact is verified against an architecture-specific pin holding the
#      SHA-512 digest of its exact bytes. Each pin is scoped to a single release so that a
#      re-pinned release never inherits the checksum of another version. Artifact retrieval
#      verifies any declared pin and aborts on a mismatch. A release without a declared pin uses
#      trust on first use: the initial retrieval logs the observed hash and records it under
#      $PX_OUT/dist/pins.env outside the source tree, and every subsequent retrieval verifies the
#      artifact against that recorded value. Copy a recorded hash into this file to promote it to
#      a declared pin.
#
# The artifact downloader in scripts/fetch-dist.sh reads one entry per artifact. The <KEY> token
# is the artifact name in uppercase with hyphens replaced by underscores, and <REL> represents the
# release version in the same form (such as 3_4_3 for 3.4.3):
#   PX_DIST_<KEY>_VERSION          the target release version of the artifact entry
#   PX_DIST_<KEY>_PATH             a relative path beneath the Apache distribution root, which the
#                                  Apache mirror service resolves over HTTPS with the Apache
#                                  archive as a fallback
#   PX_DIST_<KEY>_URL              a complete HTTPS URL for an artifact that is not distributed
#                                  through the Apache mirrors
#   PX_DIST_<KEY>_BASE_URL and     the same HTTPS URL split across two variables and joined with a
#   PX_DIST_<KEY>_FILE             slash when the full address would exceed the maximum line length
#   PX_DIST_<KEY>_<REL>_SHA512_<ARCH>
#                                  the declared SHA-512 checksum pin for one specific release
# Here <ARCH> is ARM64 or AMD64, where arm64 is the primary architecture and amd64 is supported on
# a best-effort basis. Every variable name except the checksum pin also supports variants with
# _<ARCH> appended at the end, with _<REL> inserted after <KEY>, or with both qualifiers present.
# A release-qualified variable takes precedence over an unqualified one, and an
# architecture-qualified variable then takes precedence over an architecture-neutral one. Within a
# value, the {version} token expands to the release string. Because a SHA-512 digest exceeds the
# maximum line length, a pin continues across <PIN>_2, <PIN>_3, and subsequent numbered variables,
# which retrieval concatenates in order until the assembled digest holds 128 hexadecimal digits.
#
# Never write an assignment with an empty value in this file: the configuration loader records the
# empty value at stage 6, which prevents any stage-7 assignment for that variable from taking
# effect.

# --- Artifacts -----------------------------------------------------------------
# This list defines the default set of distribution entries fetched when retrieval is invoked
# without explicit artifact names.
PX_DIST_ARTIFACTS=hbase,hadoop,async-profiler,jhiccup

# --- The Phoenix HBase profile and the HBase release ---------------------------
PX_PHOENIX_HBASE_PROFILE_DEFAULT=2.6

# Each profile maps to a default HBase runtime release. The floating 2.5 and 2.6 profiles track
# their respective minor release lines and therefore default to the latest patch release, whereas
# the remaining profiles target an older compatibility module and default to the exact release
# version configured for that profile in the root pom.xml.
PX_DIST_HBASE_DEFAULT_2_5_0=2.5.3
PX_DIST_HBASE_DEFAULT_2_5_4=2.5.10
PX_DIST_HBASE_DEFAULT_2_5=2.5.16
PX_DIST_HBASE_DEFAULT_2_6_0=2.6.1
PX_DIST_HBASE_DEFAULT_2_6_3=2.6.3
PX_DIST_HBASE_DEFAULT_2_6=2.6.7

# Because HBase publishes a single architecture-independent binary archive per release, the ARM64
# and AMD64 checksum pins for a given release record the same SHA-512 digest.
PX_DIST_HBASE_PATH=hbase/{version}/hbase-{version}-hadoop3-bin.tar.gz
PX_DIST_HBASE_2_6_7_SHA512_ARM64=2e0835a3ed8e5a9114f5d878deafb2f7a6b1c8386ba422d1a307fcc5551d452d
PX_DIST_HBASE_2_6_7_SHA512_ARM64_2=c7da468729a43acf75dcfe0b20424cb48f72ed424dfd15f81b1b3624454ed82d
PX_DIST_HBASE_2_6_7_SHA512_AMD64=2e0835a3ed8e5a9114f5d878deafb2f7a6b1c8386ba422d1a307fcc5551d452d
PX_DIST_HBASE_2_6_7_SHA512_AMD64_2=c7da468729a43acf75dcfe0b20424cb48f72ed424dfd15f81b1b3624454ed82d
PX_DIST_HBASE_2_5_16_SHA512_ARM64=d7ffcbcd8c8905f0f72af0d8c5e63ccc5221fd4cda3183a79ffe19fe89245d8d
PX_DIST_HBASE_2_5_16_SHA512_ARM64_2=8a2d3c7074ab58877a9c13dd4a9fbc3dc2ec56c7ea305082eabb02b3a7d1932f
PX_DIST_HBASE_2_5_16_SHA512_AMD64=d7ffcbcd8c8905f0f72af0d8c5e63ccc5221fd4cda3183a79ffe19fe89245d8d
PX_DIST_HBASE_2_5_16_SHA512_AMD64_2=8a2d3c7074ab58877a9c13dd4a9fbc3dc2ec56c7ea305082eabb02b3a7d1932f

# --- Hadoop --------------------------------------------------------------------
# The default Hadoop release used to run the HDFS and YARN cluster daemons across all profiles.
PX_DIST_HADOOP_DEFAULT=3.4.3

# Because Hadoop ships architecture-specific native libraries, it publishes a separate arm64
# distribution archive whose filename convention varies across releases. Each Hadoop release must
# therefore declare its own explicit arm64 distribution path, and any release lacking that path is
# rejected.
PX_DIST_HADOOP_PATH_AMD64=hadoop/common/hadoop-{version}/hadoop-{version}.tar.gz
PX_DIST_HADOOP_3_4_3_PATH_ARM64=hadoop/common/hadoop-3.4.3/hadoop-3.4.3-aarch64.tar.gz
PX_DIST_HADOOP_3_4_2_PATH_ARM64=hadoop/common/hadoop-3.4.2/hadoop-3.4.2-aarch64-lean.tar.gz
PX_DIST_HADOOP_3_4_3_SHA512_ARM64=2f5c1719b801eedecc5bbed0d4c6d61d7c4850dbb5944fb79da24474f694cb5d
PX_DIST_HADOOP_3_4_3_SHA512_ARM64_2=0f00b07d1b54cade83f6ca492e1697225f47737cc1a4478ca04102062cf314d5
PX_DIST_HADOOP_3_4_3_SHA512_AMD64=e25be7e57b4d3c5bfe83895844321a21d6cf7331266d524d8983c27cf484e576
PX_DIST_HADOOP_3_4_3_SHA512_AMD64_2=c3d79b3b60d590f8cddecf16229d0e232de2491b1b61b362ee7d67072c7290e1

# --- Profiling tools -----------------------------------------------------------
# Because async-profiler is distributed outside the Apache mirror system, its architecture-specific
# release archives are downloaded directly from the upstream project release page. To keep each
# line within the length limit, the download URL is split into a shared base URL and an
# architecture-specific relative file path that retrieval joins with a slash.
PX_DIST_ASYNC_PROFILER_VERSION=4.1
PX_DIST_ASYNC_PROFILER_BASE_URL=https://github.com/async-profiler/async-profiler/releases/download
PX_DIST_ASYNC_PROFILER_FILE_ARM64=v{version}/async-profiler-{version}-linux-arm64.tar.gz
PX_DIST_ASYNC_PROFILER_FILE_AMD64=v{version}/async-profiler-{version}-linux-x64.tar.gz

# The jHiccup distribution is compiled from its upstream source archive by
# scripts/build-jhiccup.sh, and any declared checksum pin applies to that source tarball.
PX_DIST_JHICCUP_VERSION=2.0.10
PX_DIST_JHICCUP_URL=https://github.com/giltene/jHiccup/archive/refs/tags/jHiccup-{version}.tar.gz

# --- The harness image ---------------------------------------------------------
# A single local container image serves every cluster role. The image bundles JDK 11, 17, and 21
# so that each container instance can select its active JDK at startup, and the harness never
# pulls or pushes this image during a test run. The configuration loader derives PX_IMAGE_TAG from
# the active profile alongside the selected HBase and Hadoop releases, ensuring that distinct
# version sets never share an image tag.

# Each selectable JDK is sourced from its own base image, which the Dockerfile pins by its
# architecture-specific hexadecimal SHA-256 manifest digest via PX_IMAGE_BASE_JDK<N>_SHA256_<ARCH>.
# Operators may declare these digests in versions.local.env, and the staging step supplies the
# digest matching the target build architecture. Any digest not declared in configuration follows
# a trust-on-first-use policy: the initial image build resolves the digest and records it in
# $PX_OUT/images/pins.env, while the build refuses to proceed if a base image lacks a resolved
# digest.
PX_IMAGE_BASE_JDK11=eclipse-temurin:11-jdk-noble
PX_IMAGE_BASE_JDK17=eclipse-temurin:17-jdk-noble
PX_IMAGE_BASE_JDK21=eclipse-temurin:21-jdk-noble
# PX_IMAGE_BASE_JDK11_SHA256_ARM64=<sha256>
# PX_IMAGE_BASE_JDK11_SHA256_AMD64=<sha256>
# PX_IMAGE_BASE_JDK17_SHA256_ARM64=<sha256>
# PX_IMAGE_BASE_JDK17_SHA256_AMD64=<sha256>
# PX_IMAGE_BASE_JDK21_SHA256_ARM64=<sha256>
# PX_IMAGE_BASE_JDK21_SHA256_AMD64=<sha256>

# Base JRE image for docker/pherf, which packages the Distributed Pherf controller and agents. The
# JRE must include the jdk.httpserver module, and the image build explicitly verifies its presence.
# Digest pinning follows the same policy as the JDK base images via
# PX_IMAGE_BASE_JRE17_SHA256_<ARCH>: operators may declare the digest here or in
# versions.local.env, and any undeclared digest is resolved under trust on first use.
PX_IMAGE_BASE_JRE17=eclipse-temurin:17-jre-noble
# PX_IMAGE_BASE_JRE17_SHA256_ARM64=<sha256>
# PX_IMAGE_BASE_JRE17_SHA256_AMD64=<sha256>
